# demo.sh writes its canonical evidence set directly into this directory:
#   order-service.sbom.cdx.json / order-service.grype.json
#   monolith.sbom.cdx.json      / monolith.grype.json
#   summary.txt
# Those five files ARE committed, as point-in-time evidence (the grype DB
# build date and the pinned base-image tag are the point-in-time anchors) --
# re-running demo.sh against a newer vulnerability DB or a rebuilt image is
# expected to produce a git diff on them, same as any other example's
# captured-run evidence in this project.
#
# Anything else dropped here by an ad hoc or scratch invocation should not be
# committed.
*.tmp
*.log
/scratch/
